1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,220
Social Studies, Class 5.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Lesson 2: Earth Movement.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,320
Learning Objectives.

4
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,560
By the end of this chapter,

5
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:14,620
learners will be able to:

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,460
Understand that the Earth is spherical.

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:20,940
Identify the two types of movements of

8
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:21,460
the Earth.

9
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:24,480
Explain rotation and its effects.

10
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,880
Understand revolution and its effects.

11
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,600
Learn about different seasons caused by revolution.

12
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:35,640
Define solstices and equinoxes and when they

13
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:36,040
occur.

14
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:37,940
Start-Up Activity.

15
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:41,880
Take a ball and spin it.

16
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:43,800
Notice how it moves.

17
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:47,500
Imagine this is the Earth moving in

18
00:00:47,580 --> 00:00:47,900
space.

19
00:00:49,060 --> 00:00:52,420
The Earth moves in two ways—let's explore

20
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,260
these movements and their effects!

21
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:56,960
Who proved that the earth is spherical?

22
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:02,220
Many ancient civilizations believed that the Earth

23
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:02,880
was flat.

24
00:01:03,680 --> 00:01:07,360
However, Greek philosopher Pythagoras was one of

25
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,380
the first to suggest that the Earth

26
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:10,100
is spherical.

27
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:14,760
Later, Aristotle provided evidence by observing how

28
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,680
ships disappear over the horizon and how

29
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,700
the Earth's shadow on the Moon is

30
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,540
curved during a lunar eclipse.

31
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:25,404
Ferdinand Magellan's voyage around the world further

32
00:01:25,484 --> 00:01:27,320
confirmed that the Earth is round.

33
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:30,100
The Two Movements of the Earth.

34
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:34,100
The Earth moves in two ways:

35
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,760
Rotation – The Earth spins on its

36
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,280
axis around itself.

37
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,400
Revolution – The Earth moves around the

38
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:43,800
Sun.

39
00:01:44,680 --> 00:01:45,140
Rotation.

40
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:50,240
The movement of the Earth around its

41
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:52,340
own axis is called rotation.

42
00:01:53,180 --> 00:01:55,760
The earth rotates from west to east.

43
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:59,340
It completes one full rotation in 24

44
00:01:59,420 --> 00:01:59,740
hours.

45
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:02,720
The speed of rotation is faster at

46
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:05,160
the equator and slower at the poles.

47
00:02:05,980 --> 00:02:08,160
The axis is tilted at an angle

48
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:10,634
of 23.5°.

49
00:02:10,820 --> 00:02:12,920
As the Earth is spherical in shape,

50
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:15,440
only one half of the Earth receives

51
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,680
sunlight at a time.

52
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:19,340
Thus, the side of the Earth facing

53
00:02:19,420 --> 00:02:21,260
the Sun experience day.

54
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:22,780
On the other hand,

55
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,000
the other half,

56
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,080
or the part away from the sun,

57
00:02:26,160 --> 00:02:27,560
experiences night.

58
00:02:28,280 --> 00:02:29,720
As the Earth rotates,

59
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:32,440
the lighted part moves into the darkness.

60
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:36,485
This rotation causes day and night.

61
00:02:36,565 --> 00:02:37,200
Do You Know?

62
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:41,240
The Earth rotates at a speed of

63
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:45,680
1,670 kilometers per hour at the equator,

64
00:02:46,340 --> 00:02:48,305
but we don’t feel it because we’re

65
00:02:48,385 --> 00:02:49,560
moving along with it!

66
00:02:50,200 --> 00:02:51,080
Revolution.

67
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:56,280
Revolution is the movement of the Earth

68
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,580
around the Sun in a fixed path

69
00:02:58,660 --> 00:02:59,780
called an orbit.

70
00:03:00,460 --> 00:03:02,700
The Earth revolves around the Sun in

71
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:03,900
an elliptical orbit.

72
00:03:04,540 --> 00:03:06,860
It takes three hundred and sixty-five and

73
00:03:06,940 --> 00:03:09,900
one quarter days (one year) to complete

74
00:03:09,980 --> 00:03:10,900
one revolution.

75
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,960
The tilt of the Earth's axis remains

76
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:15,760
the same during revolution.

77
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:18,780
Revolution causes seasonal changes.

78
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,480
The revolution of the Earth and the

79
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,180
tilt of its axis cause different seasons:

80
00:03:25,120 --> 00:03:27,940
Summer – The hemisphere tilted towards the

81
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,600
Sun experiences summer.

82
00:03:30,360 --> 00:03:33,240
Winter – The hemisphere tilted away from

83
00:03:33,320 --> 00:03:35,100
the Sun experiences winter.

84
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:38,840
Spring – Occurs between winter and summer

85
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,880
when the temperature starts rising.

86
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,320
Autumn – Occurs between summer and winter

87
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:46,320
when the temperature starts dropping.

88
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,260
Let's Learn More.

89
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,680
A day on Earth is actually 23

90
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,420
hours, 56 minutes,

91
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,920
not exactly 24 hours,

92
00:03:57,500 --> 00:03:59,260
but we round it off to 24

93
00:03:59,340 --> 00:04:01,560
hours because it’s easier to keep track

94
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:02,020
of time.

95
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:05,100
What is Solstice and When Does It

96
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:05,500
Occur?

97
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,900
A solstice is a day,

98
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,640
when the sun shines vertically over a

99
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:15,080
Tropic (both cancer and Capricorn) in the

100
00:04:15,160 --> 00:04:17,560
afternoon and the day is the longest

101
00:04:17,640 --> 00:04:18,720
in that hemisphere.

102
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:21,300
On the twenty-second of December,

103
00:04:21,820 --> 00:04:23,740
the rays of the sun fall directly

104
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:25,540
over the Tropic of Capricorn.

105
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,360
This is the longest day in Southern

106
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,160
Hemisphere (summer season),

107
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:32,000
while in the Northern Hemisphere,

108
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,700
it is the shortest day (winter season).

109
00:04:35,380 --> 00:04:37,400
This is called 'Winter Solstice.

110
00:04:38,260 --> 00:04:39,780
On the twenty-first of June,

111
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:42,820
sunlight falls vertically over the Tropic of

112
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:43,220
Cancer.

113
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:46,040
This is the longest day in Northern

114
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:49,555
Hemisphere and hence it is called 'Summer

115
00:04:49,647 --> 00:04:51,660
Solstice', while in the Southern Hemisphere,

116
00:04:51,740 --> 00:04:53,200
it is the shortest day.

117
00:04:53,940 --> 00:04:54,980
Let's Learn More.

118
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:59,160
Earth keeps rotating due to inertia,

119
00:04:59,960 --> 00:05:02,460
the same reason you continue moving forward

120
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:04,400
when you stop a bike suddenly.

121
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:07,920
This movement doesn’t stop because there’s no

122
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:09,940
friction in space to slow it down!

123
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:13,040
What is Equinox and When Does It

124
00:05:13,120 --> 00:05:13,440
Occur?

125
00:05:15,360 --> 00:05:17,740
The sun falls directly on the equator

126
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:19,160
two times in a year.

127
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:22,340
During this period there is equal length

128
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,380
of day and night all over the

129
00:05:24,460 --> 00:05:24,780
world.

130
00:05:25,320 --> 00:05:26,480
In Northern Hemisphere,

131
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:29,380
the March Equinox is called the Vernal

132
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:33,060
or Spring Equinox while September Equinox is

133
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,680
called Autumnal Equinox.

134
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:39,300
Spring Equinox (March 21st) marks the beginning

135
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,040
of spring.

136
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:44,660
Autumn Equinox (September 23rd) marks the beginning

137
00:05:44,740 --> 00:05:45,440
of autumn.

138
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:46,740
Recall.

139
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:50,020
The Earth's movements,

140
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,220
rotation and revolution,

141
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:55,080
have significant affects on our lives.

142
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:58,140
Rotation causes day and night,

143
00:05:58,620 --> 00:06:01,020
while revolution leads to the change of

144
00:06:01,100 --> 00:06:01,440
seasons.

145
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:05,520
Solstices and equinoxes mark the shift in

146
00:06:05,600 --> 00:06:08,380
seasons, playing an essential role in our

147
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:09,800
climate and timekeeping.

148
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:11,720
Let's Remember.

149
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:15,740
The Earth moves in two ways:

150
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:18,060
rotation and revolution.

151
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,960
Rotation causes day and night,

152
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,360
while revolution causes seasons.

153
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:27,200
The Earth completes one rotation in 24

154
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,181
hours and one revolution in three hundred

155
00:06:30,261 --> 00:06:32,600
and sixty-five and one quarter days.

156
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:36,000
Solstices occur in June and December,

157
00:06:36,420 --> 00:06:38,740
marking the longest and shortest days.

158
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,200
Equinoxes occur in March and September,

159
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:44,580
when day and night are equal.

160
00:06:45,380 --> 00:06:46,060
Word Bank.

161
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:50,740
Rotation – Spinning of the Earth on

162
00:06:50,820 --> 00:06:51,460
its axis.

163
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:55,600
Revolution – Movement of the Earth around

164
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,100
the Sun.

165
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,220
Orbit – The path of the Earth

166
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,360
around the Sun.

167
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,420
Solstice – When the Sun is at

168
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:05,940
its farthest point north or south.

169
00:07:06,740 --> 00:07:09,380
Equinox – When day and night are

170
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:09,820
equal.
